Performance & Scalability Tweaks
✅ Prevent Re-renders Even More:

Wrap setActiveTab inside useCallback() to optimize performance further.
Memoize the ActiveComponent selection using useMemo().
✅ Lazy Load Tab Buttons:

If you have tons of tabs, we can virtualize them using react-window or react-virtualized.
✅ Persist Active Tab Across Page Refresh:

Store activeTab in localStorage or URL query parameters to remember the last selected tab.
🎨 UI & UX Enhancements
✅ Animate Tab Transitions:

Use framer-motion to smoothly animate content when switching tabs.
✅ Scrollable Tabs for Many Items:

Add horizontal scrolling if there are too many tabs using overflow-x: auto.
✅ Keyboard Navigation:

Enable arrow key navigation (← →) between tabs for better accessibility.
✅ Dynamic Themes:

Make the tab UI themeable using CSS variables or styled-components.
🔹 Feature Additions
✅ Nested Tabs:

If you need sub-tabs, we can introduce a nested tab structure.
✅ Tab Content Fetching:

If tab content comes from an API, we can fetch data only when the tab is active to improve performance.
✅ Custom Closeable Tabs:

Allow users to close tabs dynamically (useful for dashboards, admin panels).
✅ Role-Based Tabs:

Show/hide specific tabs based on user roles (e.g., admin, user, guest).
